#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092218 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092060 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87f80908-037b-56ae-a2b5-59bdc49f0acb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Coordinates of a Point Given a Description of the Radius and Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "3454059c-9847-5bb2-9732-e33885afa462" :question/math-academy-id "e-5384" :question/problem "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $2,$ and that $P$ makes an angle of $135^{\\circ}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta),$ where\n\n$$\nr=2, \\quad \\theta=135^{\\circ}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx = r\\cos\\theta, \\qquad y=r\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tx &= r\\cos\\theta\\[5pt]\n\t\t &=2 \\cos\\left( 135^{\\circ} \\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 2 \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= -\\sqrt{2}\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\ty &= r\\sin\\theta\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 2 \\sin\\left(135^{\\circ}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 2 \\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= \\sqrt{2}\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $\\left(  -\\sqrt{2},  \\sqrt{2}\\right).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87f80908-037b-56ae-a2b5-59bdc49f0acb" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564654 :question-generator/id #uuid "f1aa751a-ff48-5f93-88ac-9dd8789e139c" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186092218.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87f80908-037b-56ae-a2b5-59bdc49f0acb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Coordinates of a Point Given a Description of the Radius and Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83908dd0-d198-52b3-8826-afa1429dbb50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089754} {:answer/id #uuid "9ae2cd5b-f109-5dbb-bf75-ab22f3567103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089755} {:answer/id #uuid "0c3da346-d7d9-5148-b044-6261a6a7a773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089756} {:answer/id #uuid "46f644a7-41c7-575e-90ea-b0bdf7907385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}, \\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089757} {:answer/id #uuid "4e49a3e0-69dd-5cc5-8e4e-d960cd9640b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089758}] :answer-field/id #uuid "1c74ba52-6920-5ddb-99ba-e1cd12c20908" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089753}] :question/id #uuid "a5be0c71-ace5-571a-88cf-4ce8508ffc58" :question/math-academy-id "q-17133" :question/problem "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $1$, and that $P$ makes an angle of $\\frac{5π}{3}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87f80908-037b-56ae-a2b5-59bdc49f0acb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Coordinates of a Point Given a Description of the Radius and Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a09efa26-c8e0-5412-ab88-3198ac483f85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}, 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091349} {:answer/id #uuid "b4663627-6e87-5b9e-ad2a-b45c4d9efc23"